		"notes": "\n\t<p><i>Spore-lobbing purple fungus that reproduces by infecting fleshy creatures. A common underground hazard.</i></p>\n\t<p></p>\n\t<p><strong>AC</strong> 8, <strong>HP</strong> 19, <strong>ATK</strong> 6 spore pellet (near) +2 (1d8 + inoculate), <strong>MV</strong> close, <strong>S</strong> -3, <strong>D</strong> -2, <strong>C</strong> +1, <strong>I</strong> -4, <strong>W</strong> -3, <strong>Ch</strong> -4, <strong>AL</strong> N, <strong>LV</strong> 4</p><p></p>\n\t<p><strong>Inoculate</strong>. Spore disease. CON 12+ or 1d4 CON damage (can't heal while ill). Repeat check each round; ends on success. Die at 0 CON, spawning a fully-grown phycomid in 1d4 rounds.</p><p></p><p><strong>Spore Pellet</strong>. After firing 6 spore pellets, phycomid must recharge for 1d6 rounds.</p><p></p>\n\t<p><i>Shadowfinder Complete Bestiary</i></p>",
